ATTRIBUTION & ORIGINALITY

Kataskeve3D is an in-house elementary 3D geometry diagram renderer. It is
an ORIGINAL implementation and does NOT incorporate, derive from, translate, or
copy any code from the GPL-licensed Eukleides tool (https://www.eukleides.org/)
or from the unrelated npm package "euclid.js", nor from any third-party 3D or
geometry library.

Mathematical constructions used internally (midpoint, foot of perpendicular,
circle through three points, orthocenter, line/circle intersection, etc.) are
textbook Euclidean geometry and are not subject to copyright. The implementation,
source-language design, parser, evaluator, canvas renderer, and WASM numeric
core were developed independently.

The name "Kataskeve" is the Greek κατασκευή ("construction"), the term Euclid
used in the Elements for the construction step of a proposition. Earlier working
titles (both withdrawn): "euclid" (collided with the npm package euclid.js) and
"sakuzu" (collided with the Microsoft Store UWP app "Sakuzu").
